<urn:atm:triage:finding/RRG-HERMES-FLEET-NUDGE-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RRG-HERMES-FLEET-NUDGE-001" ;
  triage:title "hermes-harness agents on rand-m5 run gateway processes that never registered a graft receiver, so ATM nudges never reach them and Colima GO dispatches sat unread until a manual nudge" ;
  triage:description "Split from RRG-GRAFT-LEASE-RESTART-001 per quality-mgr verdict at 20:20Z on 2026-09-03. Evidence gathered by fenix@rand-m5 at 20:2xZ, sanitized: graft_receiver_endpoints on rand-m5 has zero rows; loki hermes profile logs contain zero atm_graft.receiver_loop lines at any date; loki gateway process has run since 2026-08-26 with no restart, the remaining m5 hermes fleet since 2026-08-22; the daemon never logs registrations so daemon stderr is non-discriminating. Effect during the readiness run: loki accumulated 77 unread including both Colima GO dispatches and only started after Rand nudged him manually. Classification: release-readiness process and fleet-deployment gap on the rand-m5 host (gateway builds or hook installs predating the hermes-atm graft rollout), outside the PR 1143 candidate diff; PR 1143 is not gated on it. Closure evidence: confirmation of the hermes-atm wheel version and receiver hook plus native-tools plugin install state for the loki profile and one other m5 hermes profile, and, with Rand approval, a loki gateway restart showing a lease row and doctor graft_receivers entry appearing; the readiness plan step 2 host precondition should then state that the Colima host hermes gateway must show a live graft receiver in doctor before GO is dispatched. Update 21:20Z: Rand ruled that hermes does not use tmux and the roster harness for hermes agents must be hermes or nudges are never sent, so loki's own diagnosis (missing recipient pane id) is wrong and the roster harness value for every m5 hermes member is part of the closure evidence. Rand also ruled that host hermes agents must never be pointed at Colima and that Colima must run a separate hermes install with its own .hermes root inside the VM; fenix@rand-m5 paused the tiers at 21:08Z and ordered a corrected VM-internal plan. fenix@rand-m5 disclosed host changes on 2026-09-03: atm-graft plugin enabled for the skillrx profile at 21:05Z and the skillrx gateway killed at 21:07Z to reload (a fleet-record closure experiment, not tier work). The trust entry named localhost predates today (AT-era testbed setup, present since at least 2026-08-29) and is tracked as RRG-TRUST-KEY-LOOPBACK-001. Roster check 21:25Z by fenix@rand-m5: all 11 hermes-profile members of the m5 hermes team already have harness=hermes while hendrix and leonardo are recorded as harness=claude-code, which Rand corrected at 21:35Z: both are hermes agents, so those two roster rows are wrong and must be set to harness=hermes as part of closure, so the deafness is entirely the missing graft receiver (no wheel in the gateway python env, no receiver registration), which narrows closure to wheel install plus gateway restart evidence. Roster correction applied 21:40Z by fenix@rand-m5: hendrix and leonardo set to harness=hermes via teams update-member (admin edit made with a hermes-team caller context, disclosed); m5 hermes roster is now 13 of 13 harness=hermes. Remaining closure: wheel in the gateway python env and a receiver registration visible in doctor after a Rand-approved gateway restart. Update 2026-09-04T02:54Z (fenix@rand-m5 step 4a, sanitized): skillrx and loki gateways reset via launchctl kickstart; both restarted, telegram connected, one hook loaded (hermes-atm, gateway startup and shutdown events). After restart doctor graft_receivers still empty and graft_receiver_endpoints rows still 0; a test nudge to loki stayed unread after 40 seconds. The wheel hypothesis is refuted: the gateway venv (runtime-v3, python 3.11) has hermes-atm 1.4.3 and atm-graft 1.4.3 with PyGraftSession importable; the 0.1.4 wheel under the separate hermes-agent-atm venv is an older unrelated copy. The hook constructs the runtime via from_gateway_runner and calls activate_receiver with ATM_HOME, ATM_IDENTITY, ATM_TEAM, ATM_CHAT_ID and ATM_WORKSPACE_ROOT from the hook config. Code reading on the candidate at 88efc6b24: activate_graft_receiver binds the local listener and then calls announce, and an announce failure is only emitted as tracing warn under subsystem atm_graft.receiver_loop (action register_graft_receiver); neither atm-graft nor hermes-atm installs a tracing subscriber in the Python host, so the announce failure is silently dropped, which explains why gateway logs show zero receiver_loop lines rather than proving success. The receiver registration surface is identical at prerelease v1.4.10 and the candidate head, so the 1.4.10 host daemon is not the discriminator. Working hypothesis: announce cannot build its lease client (workspace root lacking the roster-resolved daemon endpoint) or the daemon rejects the registration; fleet reset (4b) correctly not started. Diagnosability gap (dropped warn) noted as a candidate follow-up finding, outside the PR 1143 diff. Update 2026-09-04T03:05Z (fenix@rand-m5 diagnostics, no host changes, sanitized): the loki hook config has all seven keys; ATM_WORKSPACE_ROOT is the user home, which holds a minimal .atm.toml (one atm table, default_team only); atm doctor from that root under the gateway venv with the hook env reports liveness running, readiness ready, client and daemon 1.4.10. A one-off under the gateway venv built exactly as from_components (PyAgentAddress, PyGraftSessionOptions, PyGraftSession, activate_receiver) RAISES AtmGraftError graft receiver readiness was not signaled within 3s, reproduced twice; the daemon log for the probe window has zero graft, lease, receiver, announce or register entries, so the failure is before any lease request, inside the local readiness wait, not a rejected announce; no new socket or file under the atm home apart from mail.db WAL churn; ATM_LOG=debug adds nothing from the native side. Consequently from_components raises on the gateway startup event and the hooks loader swallows the exception (gateway log shows only Loaded hook), which is why every restart looks clean while nothing registers. Reclassified: a hermes-atm/atm-graft receiver activation defect (or an environment precondition it does not report), not a fleet-deployment gap; root-cause pass dispatched on rand-m4. Update 2026-09-04T03:3xZ (rand-m4 root-cause pass, fix ee9b60951 on the candidate): two defects. First, the deployed gateway wheels are hermes-atm and atm-graft 1.4.3, whose receiver has no lease client at all and publishes a file endpoint record under the workspace graft directory that a 1.4.10 daemon never reads, so even a successful 1.4.3 receiver receives zero nudges; closure requires wheels rebuilt from the candidate installed into the gateway venv. Second, in atm-graft the ReceiverReadyLatch kept its own sender alive so a receive loop that died before signaling readiness still burned the full 3s deadline and 1.4.3 additionally discarded the worker error without joining it, which is exactly the bare timeout observed; ee9b60951 moves the only sender into the loop, joins the worker, and returns the typed cause (regression tests in atm-graft runtime and lib; just lint, cargo test -p atm-graft, test-graft-python and test-hermes-graft-bridge exit 0). Likely true cause on rand-m5 once diagnosable: receiver already active (a still-running gateway holding the workspace graft lock) or an unwritable graft receiver directory. Next: fenix@rand-m5 rebuilds wheels from the candidate tip, installs into the gateway venv for skillrx and loki, re-probes, resets those two gateways, reports doctor graft_receivers. Live verification on rand-m5 2026-09-04T03:5xZ (fenix@rand-m5, disclosed host changes, sanitized): wheels atm_graft 1.4.11 and hermes_atm 1.4.11 built with maturin from the candidate at 2f5486d78. Isolated venv proof first: with the loki identity the new wheels immediately return the typed cause receiver already active (lock held by the still-running 1.4.3 gateway), confirming the masking defect fixed; with an identity whose gateway was dead, activate_receiver returned, doctor showed one receiver reachable, endpoint rows 1, and close deregistered cleanly, so 1.4.11 wheels register against the unchanged 1.4.10 host daemon. Then both wheels installed into the gateway venv (no-deps, nothing else touched) and the skillrx and loki gateways reset: after 30 seconds doctor graft_receivers = 2 (both reachable), endpoint rows 2, and a test nudge to loki produced an autonomous reply within about 60 seconds with no manual prompt. Wake path proven. Fleet reset of the remaining hermes members in progress, sequential; hendrix has no gateway profile on this host (separate install) and two profiles were already dead before this work. Closure verdict is quality-mgr's." ;
